The simulator will be implemented using a combination of C++ and Python. The physics calculations will be implemented in C++, and the joystick interface will be implemented in Python using the Pygame library.

Optimization for Real-Time Performance
--------------------------------------

To optimize the simulator for real-time performance, we will use the following techniques:

*   **Multithreading**: The simulator will use multithreading to separate the physics calculations from the joystick interface. This will allow the simulator to run the physics calculations in the background while still responding to user input.
